   "category": "confirmed observable anomaly",
   "verbatim": "{\"at\":\"2026-11-24T18:54:12.815Z\",\"source\":\"kane\",\"nonceValid\":true,\"category\":\"confirmed observable anomaly\",\"rules\":\"R8\",\"builds\":\"QX-73 (comparison: QX-41)\",\"claim\":\"QX-73 did not consume a +1 action cell after entry. The same AI piece entered I5 via shove, then stepped off and re-entered; the cell fired twice and granted two extra actions. R8 says an effect fires on arrival and is then used up, including effect-driven arrival.\",\"evidence\":\"C-9fc650 (QX-73), turn 4, steps 11 and 13: I5 +1 action fires at both entries and remains after step 11. Compare C-757669 (QX-41), turn 4, step 11: I5 is removed after the first entry; its later move I5 left is refused after actions run out.\",\"reproduce\":\"Run the scripted forced-entry +1 case on QX-73: place Shove west 2 at K5 and +1 action at I5; move AI M5-L5-K5 so shove forces it to I5; move I5-H5-I5. Verify I5 disappears immediately after the first effect-fired event and cannot fire again.\",\"suggestion\":\"Consume/remove the effect cell atomically on its first firing, including chained or forced arrivals. Add a regression asserting one effect-fired event for I5 and no extra action on re-entry.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"nonce\":\"d9b7417e6ecb2a0c\"}",
