   "verbatim": "{\"at\":\"2026-11-24T18:54:34.743Z\",\"source\":\"kane\",\"nonceValid\":true,\"category\":\"confirmed observable anomaly\",\"rules\":\"R3\",\"builds\":\"QX-73 (comparison: QX-41)\",\"claim\":\"QX-73 grants Human four starting move actions while all three Human pieces remain on the board. R3 specifies one move action per own piece, so the observed starting allowance should be three. QX-41 grants three in the matching script.\",\"evidence\":\"C-9fc650 (QX-73), turn 1 step 1: turn-start side=Human actionsGranted=4 with h1, h2, h3 all on board; also turn 3 step 6 and turn 5 step 15 show Human actionsGranted=4. Matching C-757669 (QX-41), turn 1 step 1, records actionsGranted=3.\",\"reproduce\":\"Start the forced-entry +1 scripted case on QX-73 without any prior +1 action effect. At Human turn 1, count the three Human pieces and compare the turn-start actionsGranted value; it should equal three.\",\"suggestion\":\"Initialize turn actions from the current count of the side's pieces on the board, with only a valid +1 effect modifying that allowance. Add a test asserting actionsGranted=3 for the three-piece initial state.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"nonce\":\"d9b7417e6ecb2a0c\"}",
